"{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1371/journal.pone.0009506\",\n  \"title\": \"Statistical Analysis of the Indus Script Using n-Grams\",\n  \"authors\": \"Nisha Yadav; Hrishikesh Joglekar; Rajesh P. N. Rao; Mayank N. Vahia; Ronojoy Adhikari; Iravatham Mahadevan\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1371/journal.pone.0009506\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2010-03-19T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0009506\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 25,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Public Library of Science (PLoS)', 'container_title': 'PLoS ONE', 'volume': '5', 'issue': '3', 'page': 'e9506', 'issn': ['1932-6203'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '340', 'prefix': '10.1371'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.16943/ijhs/2019/v54i2/49656\",\n  \"title\": \"Structure of Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"Nisha Yadav\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.16943/ijhs/2019/v54i2/49656\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2019-07-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"http://insa.nic.in/writereaddata/UpLoadedFiles/IJHS/Vol54_2_2019__Art01.pdf\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.16943/ijhs/2019/v54i2/49656\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Indian National Science Academy', 'container_title': 'Indian Journal of History of Science', 'volume': '54', 'issue': '2', 'page': '', 'issn': ['0019-5235'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '6718', 'prefix': '10.16943'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1515/9783110800258.39\",\n  \"title\": \"THE POSITIONAL-STATISTICAL ANALYSIS OF THE PROTO-INDIAN TEXTS\",\n  \"authors\": \"A. M. KONDRATOV\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1515/9783110800258.39\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1976-12-31T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1515/9783110800258.39\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 1,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'DE GRUYTER', 'container_title': 'The Soviet Decipherment of the Indus Valley Script', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '39-54', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '374', 'prefix': '10.1515'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvzgb7m5.8\",\n  \"title\": \"The Buddhist Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvzgb7m5.8\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2020-03-26T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvzgb7m5.8\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Harrassowitz Verlag', 'container_title': 'The Buddhist Indus Script and Scriptures', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '9-64', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.7717/peerj.7844/supp-2\",\n  \"title\": \"Supplemental Information 2: Script Statistical Analysis: R Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.7717/peerj.7844/supp-2\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1970-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj.7844/supp-2\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"component\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'PeerJ', 'container_title': '', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'component', 'member': '4443', 'prefix': '10.7717'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.59720/22-256\",\n  \"title\": \"Statistical models for identifying missing and unclear signs of the Indus script\",\n  \"authors\": \"Varun Venkatesh; Ali Farghaly\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>A writing system was developed between 2500 and 1800 BCE in the Indus Valley civilization in the Indian subcontinent and remains undeciphered. Indus script texts found so far in the archeological digs from this civilization are limited in number and include a lot of damaged artifacts with missing and unclear signs. Identifying the missing and unclear signs and extending the Indus text corpus will aid the researchers in deciphering this script. This work aimed to predict the missing and unclear signs using n-gram Markov chain models using the Interactive Corpus of Indus Texts (ICIT) text corpus. First, we analyzed patterns and concordances of the signs, pairs, triplets, and other n-grams and discovered the positional behavior of signs in the Indus texts. With that understanding, we built Markov chain language models based on n-grams, augmented with sign positional probabilities. Since signs could be missing in any location of the texts, we devised and implemented effective sign fill-in algorithms on top of these Markov chain models. Using the language models and the sign fill-in algorithms, we tuned our models and predicted single signs that were deliberately removed from complete texts with about 63% accuracy. Then we used the best model and our tuned parameters to predict missing and unclear single signs in about 100 texts. The statistical methods we described here improve our understanding of the Indus script. Filling in the missing signs makes the corpus more complete and helps contribute to the broader decipherment effort.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.59720/22-256\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2023-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.59720/22-256\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 2,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'The Journal of Emerging Investigators, Inc.', 'container_title': 'Journal of Emerging Investigators', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '39001', 'prefix': '10.59720'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"title\": \"The Indus Valley Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2015-02-06T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'The Archaeology and Epigraphy of Indus Writing', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '4-12', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1080/09296174.2017.1406294\",\n  \"title\": \"Statistical Analysis of the Tables in Mahadevan’s Concordance of the Indus Valley Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"Michael Philip Oakes\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1080/09296174.2017.1406294\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2017-12-06T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1080/09296174.2017.1406294\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 3,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Informa UK Limited', 'container_title': 'Journal of Quantitative Linguistics', 'volume': '26', 'issue': '1', 'page': '22-47', 'issn': ['0929-6174', '1744-5035'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '301', 'prefix': '10.1080'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2139/ssrn.4900721\",\n  \"title\": \"Deciphering Indus script and Pashupati Seal of Indus Valley Civilization\",\n  \"authors\": \"Shahbaig Kahoor Khan\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>Indus Valley Civilization is one of the left out archaeological treasures, that is being ignored in the recent times. This paper is a guide to the scholars and the archaeologist, which will help them to solve the mysteries of the ancient Indus Civilization and its Script. The paper includes thorough research observations on the interpretation of the scripts. Among the script and the famous Pashupati seal has also been thoroughly interpreted and explained. This could be a guide to interpret Indus customs and culture more nearer to the truth of past. The political controversies altering the history of Indus can cause a tremendous if not correctly study.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2139/ssrn.4900721\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2024-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4900721\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"posted-content\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 1,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Elsevier BV', 'container_title': '', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'posted-content', 'member': '78', 'prefix': '10.2139'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"title\": \"Sanskrit Influence on the Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jeyakumar Ramasami\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2025-12-20T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'International Journal of Science and Research', 'container_title': 'International Journal of Science and Research (IJSR)', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '1329-1334', 'issn': ['2319-7064'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '8810', 'prefix': '10.21275'}\"\n}"
